# The source file of this conversion, pinned.
#
# convert_csf.py reads it from sources/nist/ (git-ignored). The Validators
# workflow downloads it from the base below, checks it against this list
# with `sha256sum -c`, runs the converter and fails if the conversion in this
# folder comes out different. The bundle and the two coverage reports are
# therefore a reproducible record: a change of the kernel, of
# oscal_conv_lib.py or of the converter that would alter them is noticed.
#
# The base is the publisher's repository at commit 9402f031, the commit the
# IFA conversion is pinned to as well.
#
# base: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/usnistgov/oscal-content/9402f031489092246f2c27391bad452b85604140/
# into: sources/nist
# path: nist.gov/CSF/v2.0/json/NIST_CSF_v2.0_catalog.json
#
4836943f21d393f2821df85ada4e6f3c0617243b4ddf44263fe68205400210b4  NIST_CSF_v2.0_catalog.json
